UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Kansas City, Missouri, trueCABLE operates as a supplier of branded networking infrastructure products. The company focuses on delivering Ethernet and fiber optic cabling solutions directly to installers and end users.

The product range spans bulk Ethernet cable in Cat5e, Cat6, and Cat6A categories, all constructed with solid bare-copper conductors. The catalog also includes fiber optic patch cables in OS2, OM3, and OM4 configurations, a line of termination connectors (RJ45 pass-through, keystone jacks, toolless variants), patch panels in shielded and unshielded versions, and a suite of installation tools backed by a lifetime warranty. Orders placed by 3 p.m. Central Time ship the same day.

The company also serves satellite and coax installations through its bulk coax cable line. Technical guidance is provided through an online resource library called The Cable Academy.

trueCABLE differentiates itself by testing every product to exceed UL, ANSI/TIA, and RoHS standards, offering a 30-day money-back guarantee, and providing a Forever Warranty on its branded tools. The company emphasizes a system approach where cable, connectors, and tools are validated to work together in the field.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','UL Listed','ANSI/TIA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bulk Ethernet cable distribution (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6A)", "Fiber optic patch cable supply (OS2, OM3, OM4)", "Connector and termination supply (RJ45, keystone, toolless)", "Patch panel supply (shielded/unshielded, rack/wall mount)", "Network installation tool supply with lifetime warranty", "Technical training via Cable Academy online resources"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Commercial office construction", "Industrial facilities", "Residential networking", "Low-voltage contracting", "Satellite and coax installations", "Fiber optic communications"], "materials": ["Solid bare copper", "Fiber optic (OS2, OM3, OM4)", "PVC/plenum-rated cable jackets", "Coaxial cable with solid bare copper conductors"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on orders placed by 3 p.m. CT", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on orders placed by 3 p.m. CT", "Forever Warranty on branded installation tools", "30-day money-back guarantee on all products", "Products tested to exceed UL, ANSI/TIA, and RoHS standards", "Cable, connector, and tool ecosystem validated for interoperability"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Kansas City, Missouri -> db", "Certifications: ROHS, UL Listed -> db", "Same-day shipping by 3pm CT -> /", "Forever Warranty on tools -> /", "30-day money-back guarantee -> /", "Product lines: Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6A Ethernet cable, fiber patch cables, connectors, tools, patch panels -> /", "Industries: data centers, offices, industrial, commercial, residential, low-voltage, satellite -> /", "Materials: solid bare copper, fiber optic OS2/OM3/OM4, coax with solid bare copper -> /", "Compliance: UL, ANSI/TIA, RoHS -> /", "System approach: cable, connectors, tools validated to work together -> /", "Cable Academy technical resources -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "From bulk Ethernet and fiber cable to terminations and tools, trueCABLE delivers professional-grade products designed for seamless installs and rock-solid performance.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='truecable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='10 Men Metal Fabrication operates from Omaha, Nebraska, where it was established in 2019 by owner and president Jaco Germishuys. The company began with a vision to serve as a one-stop shop for architectural sheet metal and custom fabrication, regardless of project size or complexity.

The shop specializes in architectural sheet metal fabrication for metal roofing systems, providing services such as shearing, folding, welding, perforating, and metal finishing. Its fully equipped metal shop produces standing seam panels, custom trim, vented ridge caps, column covers, cornice metal, gutters, downspouts, conductor heads, scuppers, and specialty items like copper and zinc countertops and backsplashes. The team brings 38 years of combined industry experience and has completed over 500 projects.

Customers include contractors, architects, homeowners, and DIY enthusiasts primarily across the Midwest. The company works with professionals in the construction industry as well as residential clients seeking custom architectural metal components.

