UPDATE companies SET description='ABE Equipment is headquartered in Lincoln, Nebraska. The company traces its roots to Norland International, a turnkey beverage equipment supplier with nearly three decades of experience. In 2020, the business rebranded from American Beer Equipment to ABE Beverage Equipment, and in 2022 shortened its name to ABE Equipment to reflect a broader market focus beyond beverages. No founding year or ownership structure is publicly disclosed.

The company designs and assembles complete beverage production systems, including brewhouses, canning lines, distillation equipment, cellar tanks, filling machines, keg cleaners, labelers, and auxiliary packaging items. Operations are housed on a 140,000‑square‑foot campus that encompasses fabrication, production, warehousing, and support functions. A staff of 135 includes degreed electrical and mechanical engineers, a ten‑person customer service team that also serves as training technicians, and sales personnel with a combined 80 years of industry experience.

ABE serves craft beverage producers across categories such as craft beer, craft spirits, kombucha, cider, cold‑brew coffee, seltzer, infused beverages, craft soda, and wine. Customers range from startup entrepreneurs to established businesses expanding production capacity. The company positions itself as a single source for turnkey solutions, custom engineering, startup assistance, and ongoing parts support.

ABE emphasizes a service‑driven differentiator: its customer service representatives double as training technicians, ensuring hands‑on knowledge of both equipment and processes. Free equipment layout services, in‑house engineering, and a large parts warehouse are cited as key advantages. Core values highlighted by the company include adaptability, dedication, integrity, reliability, and respectfulness.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Turnkey beverage equipment systems", "Equipment layout and design", "Electrical and mechanical engineering", "Equipment fabrication and assembly", "Startup and training services", "Ongoing customer support and maintenance", "Parts warehouse and replacement parts", "Custom equipment customization"], "industries": ["Craft Beer", "Craft Spirits", "Kombucha", "Cider", "Cold Brew Coffee", "Seltzer", "Infused Beverages", "Craft Soda", "Wine"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Brewhouses", "Microbrewery Equipment", "Distillery Equipment", "Micro Distillery Equipment", "Cellar Tanks & Controls", "Filling Equipment", "Canning Lines", "Keg Cleaning", "Multi-Use Labelers", "Production Auxiliary Items", "Packaging Auxiliary Items"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer service team of 10 who also serve as training technicians", "Degreed electrical and mechanical engineers on staff", "Free equipment layout and design services", "Sales team with 80 years of combined industry experience", "140,000 sq. ft. campus with fabrication, production, and warehousing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lincoln, Nebraska -> /", "Parent company Norland International with nearly 30 years experience -> /about", "Rebranded from American Beer Equipment to ABE Beverage Equipment in 2020 -> /about", "Dropped ''Beverage'' from name in 2022 -> /about", "Designs and assembles brewhouses, canning lines, distillation equipment -> /", "140,000 sq. ft. campus -> /", "135 employees including degreed engineers -> /a