UPDATE companies SET description='American Electric Equipment, Inc. (AEEI) and its sister division Control Products, Inc. (CPI) have operated from Beckley, West Virginia since 1985. The American‑owned company began with a focus on mining and underground power distribution, growing over four decades into a two‑division operation serving industrial and mining customers across the region.

The company designs and builds custom dry‑type transformers, high‑voltage switchgear (including its own ISOVAC 800 15 kV/800 A vacuum breaker and ProVac medium‑voltage breaker), explosion‑proof enclosures, control stations and junction boxes, ground monitors, power centers, substations and mining‑grade plugs and receptacles. It also reconditions Yaskawa SF6 gas circuit breakers (5–15 kV) with factory‑trained technicians, sells and services Kohler standby generators, and runs an OMAX 120X abrasive waterjet with a 26''8″ × 10′ work envelope for cutting steel, stainless, aluminum, titanium, composites, glass and stone. Additional services include on‑site metal fabrication, excavation, construction, demolition, erosion control, site reclamation, and field repair and commissioning.

Primary customers are underground and surface mining operations, industrial plants requiring custom power distribution, and commercial/industrial facilities needing standby generation. Examples include ground monitors and fault relays for gassy underground mines, custom power centers for underground mining and surface industrial use, and explosion‑proof control stations for hazardous locations.

The company emphasizes its American‑owned roots, deep mining‑sector expertise, and the combination of engineering and manufacturing staff that allows custom equipment to be built to exact specifications. It also highlights its authorized Kohler dealer status and Yaskawa‑trained service technicians as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom dry-type transformer manufacturing", "High-voltage switchgear manufacturing (ISOVAC 800, ProVac)", "Explosion-proof enclosure, control station, and junction box manufacturing", "Ground monitor and fault device manufacturing", "Power center and substation manufacturing", "Mining-grade plug, receptacle, and contactor manufacturing", "Yaskawa SF6 circuit breaker reconditioning and repair", "Kohler standby generator sales, sizing, installation, and service", "OMAX 120X abrasive waterjet cutting", "On-site and in-house metal fabrication", "Excavation, construction, and demolition", "Erosion control and site reclamation", "Field service (on-site repair and commissioning)", "Engineering and repair (breaker repairs, transformer servicing, field testing)", "Custom power distribution system design", "Motor starter manufacturing", "Capacitor trip device manufacturing"], "industries": ["Mining (underground and surface)", "Industrial power distribution", "Commercial standby power", "Industrial standby power", "Hazardous location / gassy mining environments"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Titanium", "Composites", "Glass", "Stone"], "equipment": ["OMAX 120X abrasive waterjet", "ISOVAC 800 vacuum isolation breaker", "ProVac vacuum circuit breaker", "Yaskawa SF6 circuit breakers (reconditioned)", "Kohler standby generators"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American owned and operated", "Two divisions: AEEI electrical equipment and CPI explosion\u2011proof products", "OMAX 120X waterjet with 26''8\u2033 \u00d7 10\u2032 cutting envelope", "Yaskawa\u2011trained technicians for SF6 breaker reconditioning and repair", "Authorized Kohler generator dealer with full sales, installation and service"], "facts_used": ["Company name, founding year 1985, headquarters Beckley WV -> db", "Two divisions AEEI and CPI -> /", "Custom transformers, switchgear, explosion-proof equipment, Yaskawa SF6 breakers -> /", "ISOVAC 800 15kV 800A vacuum breaker -> /", "ProVac vacuum circuit breaker -> /", "Explosion-proof enclosures, control stations, junction boxes -> /", "Ground monitors, fault relays, splitters -> /", "Power centers, substations, motor starters -> /", "Mining-grade plugs, receptacles, DC contactors, capacitor trip devices -> /", "Yaskawa SF6 breaker reconditioning 5-15kV, factory-tested, Yaskawa-trained techs -> /", "Kohler generator authorized dealer, sales, installation, service -> /", "OMAX 120X waterjet, 26''8\" x 10'' work area, cuts steel, stainless, aluminum, titanium, composites, glass, stone -> /", "On-site and in-house metal fabrication -> /", "Excavation, construction, demolition, erosion control, site reclamation -> /", "Field service, engineering, repair -> /", "Industries: mining, industrial, commercial/industrial standby -> /", "American owned and operated -> /", "Deep expertise in underground power distribution -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For 40 years, American Electric Equipment Inc. & Control Products Inc. have delivered custom transformers, switchgear, explosion-proof equipment, and Yaskawa high-voltage breakers to mining and industrial operations across the region.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-electric-equipment-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Woodwork Industry, LLC operates as a custom 3D laminate door manufacturer in Fort Pierce, Florida. The company has been in business for over ten years, serving the local area and beyond with thermofoil door and cabinet products.

The shop produces custom 3D laminate doors—often referred to as thermofoil doors—in a variety of profiles including shaker, slab, arch, and beaded styles, along with matching edge profiles and accessories. It also manufactures custom European frameless cabinets. Customers select a door style, choose a color from a catalog of woodgrain and solid finishes, and submit measurements via an emailed order form. The company describes its team as small and emphasizes quick turnaround on orders.

The product line targets both residential and commercial projects. Residential applications include kitchen cabinetry, bathroom vanities, closet systems, and entertainment centers. Commercial work covers any thermofoil need in non‑residential settings. The company does not list specific industry certifications or high‑volume production metrics, positioning itself as a local source for custom runs rather than a mass‑production supplier.

