UPDATE companies SET description='ASM, based in Phoenix, Arizona, has been pursuing materials innovation for nearly 60 years, according to the company. The firm does not publicly disclose its exact founding year, founders, or ownership structure.

The company designs and manufactures advanced wafer processing equipment used by semiconductor manufacturers. Its core processes include atomic layer deposition (ALD), epitaxy, chemical vapor deposition (CVD), plasma-enhanced CVD (PECVD), surface modification, and chemical mechanical planarization (CMP). ASM employs over 4,800 people across 15 key locations worldwide and targets revenue exceeding €5.7 billion by 2030.

ASM serves the semiconductor industry, with a focus on logic and foundry customers, DRAM and high-bandwidth memory (HBM) producers, and advanced packaging applications. Its technologies also support emerging sectors such as artificial intelligence, next-generation healthcare, cloud computing, and energy-efficient devices.

ASM differentiates itself through its mastery of thin-film deposition at the atomic scale, a strategy it calls ''materials purpose, engineering, and scale.'' The company maintains long-standing R&D partnerships with IMEC (since 1990) and the University of Helsinki (since 2003), and emphasizes an AI/ML-enabled common platform to accelerate innovation while reducing precursor and energy consumption.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Atomic layer deposition (ALD)", "Epitaxy", "Chemical vapor deposition (CVD)", "Plasma-enhanced CVD (PECVD)", "Surface modification", "Chemical mechanical planarization (CMP)", "Surface preparation", "Chemistry innovation", "Surface engineering", "Outcome-based services", "Service products"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Logic/foundry", "Memory (DRAM/HBM)", "Advanced packaging", "Artificial intelligence (AI)", "Healthcare", "Cloud computing", "Energy-efficient devices"], "materials": ["Flowable Carbon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Mastery of thin-film deposition at atomic scale", "Strategic R&D partnerships with IMEC (since 1990) and University of Helsinki (since 2003)", "AI/ML-enabled common platform for accelerated innovation", "Focus on chemical effectiveness and reduced precursor/energy consumption", "Outcome-based services improving uptime, yield, and performance in high-volume manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["HQ Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Nearly 60 years of innovation -> /", "4800+ employees worldwide -> /about", "15 key locations -> /about", "70+ nationalities -> /about", "58 years of research -> /about", "Partnership with IMEC since 1990 -> db", "Partnership with University of Helsinki since 2003 -> db", "Core processes: ALD, epitaxy, CVD, surface modification -> /about", "Revenue target >\u20ac5.7B by 2030 -> /about", "Industries: logic/foundry, DRAM/HBM, advanced packaging -> /about", "End markets: AI, healthcare, cloud computing, ene